t rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Joe Wilson (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Joe Wilson, the Republican incumbent since 2001, is seeking reelection in a South Carolina district that leans about seven points Republican. His Democratic challenger, 25-year-old political newcomer Zyon Khalifa, won a runoff primary in June and has emphasized his local roots and military service, but his campaign has raised under $20,000 and reported only a few hundred dollars on hand. Wilson has raised more than $860,000 and holds a substantial cash advantage.\n\nNo public general-election polling is available for this race, so the outlook rests on district fundamentals, fundraising, and expert assessments. Most national raters call the race Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-ten chance. The race draws some local coverage but shows few signs of genuine competitiveness heading into November.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0664, "margin": -9.56}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0576, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0526, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0819, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0438, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0396, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0537, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0392, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0515, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0498, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0541, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0624, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0587, "margin": -10.5}]}